From: MOOS maintainers <moos@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] setup: select the mapped image for whole regular-file disks

For an image build, the directory containing core.img belongs to the build
host, not to the target disk. Do not guess/probe that host's root device when
the destination is a whole, regular-file disk in the explicit device map.
Use the same mapped image as the root device instead. Keep GRUB's GPT embedding
algorithm, filesystem safety checks and refusal of blocklist installs intact.
Block-device and partition installation behavior remains unchanged.

This is a MOOS-local build-tool patch for GRUB 2.12, not a runtime change.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MOOS regular-file image build integration]
---
 util/setup.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/util/setup.c b/util/setup.c
--- a/util/setup.c
+++ b/util/setup.c
@@ -313,6 +313,23 @@ SETUP (const char *dir,
 
   core_dev = dest_dev;
 
+#ifdef GRUB_SETUP_BIOS
+  /* A whole regular-file image is independent of the build host's root. */
+  const char *image_path = dest_dev->disk
+    ? grub_util_biosdisk_get_osdev (dest_dev->disk) : NULL;
+  struct stat image_stat;
+  if (image_path && !dest_dev->disk->partition
+      && lstat (image_path, &image_stat) == 0
+      && S_ISREG (image_stat.st_mode))
+    {
+      root = xstrdup (dest);
+      root_dev = grub_device_open (root);
+      if (!root_dev)
+        grub_util_error ("%s", grub_errmsg);
+      grub_util_info ("using mapped regular image `%s' as root device", root);
+    }
+  else
+#endif
   {
     char **root_devices = grub_guess_root_devices (dir);
     char **cur;
